WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.480
BETH: Reasonable adjustments are a
way of ensuring that every individual

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.250
with autism has equal access to
services and facilities, by reducing

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.139
or alleviating disadvantage.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.029
Some services may need to provide
more suitable support to individuals

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.699
with autism, in order for them to
achieve the same outcomes as others.

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:22.519
Each individual with autism spectrum
disorder is unique, with different needs

00:00:23.759 --> 00:00:32.379
and challenges, therefore a comprehensive
assessment may need to be carried out,

00:00:32.379 --> 00:00:32.449
to identify their specific areas of need.

00:00:32.449 --> 00:00:36.610
JOE: The Equality Act 2010 requires
reasonable adjustments to be made, so as

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:41.390
to avoid individuals with a disability
being put at a "substantial disadvantage"

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.871
compared with those without a disability.

00:00:43.871 --> 00:00:46.765
This also applies to
individuals with autism.

00:00:46.765 --> 00:00:51.726
BETH: All service providers and public
bodies have a duty, to ensure that

00:00:51.726 --> 00:00:55.447
individuals with autism, have equal
access to healthcare, education,

00:00:55.447 --> 00:00:59.582
leisure and all other services
regardless of their specific needs.

00:00:59.582 --> 00:01:03.716
Therefore, if they cannot access
those services and facilities, then

00:01:04.129 --> 00:01:06.460
reasonable adjustments need to be made.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.239
JOE: To benefit individuals with
autism, reasonable adjustments,

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.419
should be relevant to their needs.

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:17.320
Some adjustments may be straightforward
or simple, others may be more complex.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:21.580
This may involve things like
lighting, ambient noise, visual

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:24.140
aids, quiet rooms and easy access.

00:01:24.559 --> 00:01:28.479
BETH: Some reasonable adjustments can
be done quite easily and cheaply, some

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:38.213
may be more involved and costly, but it
is important that they should be made if

00:01:38.213 --> 00:01:38.234
they benefit the individuals with autism.

